h=J.Om(a8,new A.aTz())?"Write the study guide for the material above.\nPart of the material is the written-out recording of the doctor's lecture (the file whose name starts with \ud83c\udfa7):\n- It is the main source: cover EVERYTHING taught in it, without skipping any point, example or side remark.\n- Speech jumps around: arrange it into a logical order with clear sections, and join what was said about one topic in\n  different minutes. Fix words that were clearly misheard, using the subject's context.\n- [\u0645\u0647\u0645] lines go to the \ud83c\udfaf and \ud83d\udea8 boxes. [\u0627\u0645\u062a\u062d\u0627\u0646] lines go to \ud83d\udea8 boxes and the Sheet's traps. [\u0645\u062b\u0627\u0644] lines go to\n  # Examples, step by step. [\u0648\u0627\u062c\u0628] and any exam date, format or grades go to a card \"\ud83d\udce2 \u0643\u0644\u0627\u0645 \u0645\u0647\u0645 \u0645\u0646 \u0627\u0644\u062f\u0643\u062a\u0648\u0631\".\n- Leave out [\u0645\u0634 \u0648\u0627\u0636\u062d] guesses rather than inventing what was said, and leave out the time marks. There are no slides\n  in a recording, so don't write slide references for what comes only from it.\n- When there are also slides or files: use their terms and structure, and add what the doctor said on top. Mark what\n  only the doctor said, which often comes in the exam, with \"\ud83c\udfa4 \u0627\u0644\u062f\u0643\u062a\u0648\u0631 \u0642\u0627\u0644:\".\n\n":"Write the study guide for the material above.\n"
